# netsurf: blocks inserted or removed among mixed siblings, locally (patch 377)
# Generated 2026-11-06
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 376)
#
# The r101 census: youtube's "parent holds more than blocks" (5). A
# temporary trace: youtube's <body> holds a block, a flex <div> and a line
# of inline content (a hidden 0x0 <iframe>); guardian's <body> a line of
# <gu-island> custom elements among its blocks. html_rl_block_change (the
# insert/remove path) took only parents of blocks and float carriers, and
# was entered only when the FIRST child was a block -- a <body> that starts
# with a table went to the line path and declined there.
#
#  - Flex, grid and table element boxes among the blocks are tracked like
#    blocks (one whose element left is a removal, with the same
#    object/frame checks), and the page is laid out whole.
#  - An anonymous inline container among the blocks stays as it is if
#    every element it holds is still in the parent (html_rl_ic_intact;
#    text directly in the parent declines on its own), page laid out
#    whole; the DOM walk accepts an inline element whose box is in one.
#  - Declined: a new block whose element neighbours are in the same line
#    container (it would split the line: a full build makes two); a
#    removal that leaves two line containers side by side (a full build
#    makes one line of them); an element gone from a line container.
#  - Elements that never have a box (script, style, link, meta, template,
#    title, base, noscript) are skipped in the DOM walk: a <script> in
#    <body> read as a new block (unit 362's shape).
#  - The path is entered when the block holds any block-level child
#    (html_rl_has_block_child), not only a block first.
#  - A new box is normalised by its type (html_rl_normalise_new): a new
#    element can be a flex, grid or table box by its CSS, and
#    box_normalise_block asserted on one (gate377 aborted: a shown
#    display:flex <div> among <body>'s mixed children; latent before, for
#    a display:flex <div> inserted among plain blocks). Not normalised ->
#    the full reconvert (the tree is whole), where the old code laid out
#    an unnormalised box; a non-block new box -> the page laid out whole.
#
# Result on a 2500-paragraph sim page whose <body> holds tables, a flex and
# a line of inline content: a block inserted into it, or removed,
# 103 -> 15 ms.
#
--- a/content/handlers/html/html.c
+++ b/content/handlers/html/html.c
